1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,480
快点 出门啦
Come on, let's go.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,466
我们要早点去 预留点多一点时间
We're gonna need a little more time

3
00:00:04,466 --> 00:00:05,113
过机场的安检 因为我确信
at the airport security because I'm pretty sure

4
00:00:05,113 --> 00:00:07,252
他们肯定会多留你一会儿
that they're gonna wanna patch you down.

5
00:00:07,252 --> 00:00:10,120
曼尼这周末在他爸爸那
Manny is with his father for the weekend

6
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,320
所以我和杰要飞去拉斯维加斯度周末
so Jay and I are flying to Vegas.

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:15,280
我有点左右为难 因为我既想和歌洛莉亚过二人世界
I'm a little torn because I want alone time with Gloria,

8
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:18,080
又想揉揉曼尼的头 求得在赌场的好手气
but I also like rubbing Manny's head for good luck.

9
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,943
我得给克莱尔发封邮件
I just need to send this e-mail to Claire

10
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,020
解释一下我为什么不参加下周的糕饼义卖了
why I'm not working on the bake sale next week,

11
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:25,040
但我又不能告诉她真正的原因
but I can't say the real reason.

12
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:25,640
为什么
Why not?

13
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,160
因为每次她负责这些事的时候
Because she drives me crazy

14
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,860
都让我很抓狂
when she's in charge of these things.

15
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:31,540
好吧 我们还要赶飞机 所以我就来帮帮你吧
Okay. We got a flight to catch, so let me help you out here.

16
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:31,840
好
Okay.

17
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,840
把你想跟她说的话告诉我
You tell me what you want to say to her,

18
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,060
我帮你改的委婉一些
and I'll help you find a nice way to say it.

19
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,980
我想说
I want to say...

20
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:39,920
我不能去参加糕饼义卖了
I can't work on the bake sale

21
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:42,500
因为你是一个专横的控制狂
because you're a bossy control freak

22
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,200
还瞧不上我做的纸杯蛋糕
that looks down on my cupcakes

23
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,820
虽然你自己做的柠檬方形蛋糕干的要命
even though your lemon squares were very dry.

24
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:51,420
写好了 快吧
Done. Okay?

25
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,220
你看这个怎么样
How's this?

26
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,420
亲爱的克莱尔 我不能参加糕饼义卖了
"Dear claire, I can't work the bake sale

27
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:58,940
因为你是一个专横的控制狂 还瞧不上
because you're a bossy control freak who look down --"

28
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:00,420
真幽默 杰
Very funny, Jay.

29
00:01:01,222 --> 00:01:03,485
我 我 刚才那呼呼的声音是怎么回事
I -- I -- why the whoosh?

30
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:05,241
哪去了 电子邮件哪去了
Where is -- where is the e-mail?

31
00:01:05,251 --> 00:01:07,900
已经发送了 把它弄回来
It sended! Ay. Make it come back.

32
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,260
我不知道怎么把它弄回来
I don't know how to make it come back.

33
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:10,356
这下她会看到这封邮件
Now she's gonna read it,

34
00:01:10,356 --> 00:01:12,000
然后认为是我写的
and she's gonna think it's from me!

35
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,480
严格来说 确实是你写的
Well, technically, it was from you.

36
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:14,900
走吧 出发了
Come on, let's hit the road.

37
00:01:16,069 --> 00:01:18,881
已经发送了
It sended.

38
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,040
求求你回来吧
Please come back.

39
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:37,800
我们很喜欢这个街区 但有时候
We love our neighborhood, but sometimes the last thing

40
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,080
最讨厌的事是在堵了半天车 好不容易开回家之后
you want to do after fighting traffic

41
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,800
还得再开车出门吃饭
is get back in the car to go out to eat.

42
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,400
而步行范围内唯一的一家餐馆
And the only restaurant within walking distance

43
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,976
是沙威玛城
is Shawarma City.

44
00:01:44,976 --> 00:01:47,517
两个沙威玛套餐 要猪肉还是鸡肉
Two Shawarma combo. Meat or chicken?

45
00:01:47,517 --> 00:01:48,960
一个猪肉 一个鸡肉
Uh, one meat. One chicken.

46
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,920
鸡肉那份能不能都用白肉啊
And can you make the chicken all white meat?

47
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,340
三十二号 收银柜台付款
Number 32. Pay cashier.

48
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:53,320
好吧 你根本没回答我嘛
Okay, that's not an answer.

49
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,940
然后 奇迹发生了
Then a miracle happened.

50
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:00,740
城里最热门的新餐馆
Uh, the hottest new restaurant in the city

51
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:02,220
阿米莉亚 在两个街区外
opened up two blocks away --

52
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:02,900
开了一家分店
Amelia's.

53
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,440
但有个问题
But there was a problem.

54
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:06,400
五点十五分有位子
They can take us at 5:15...

55
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,160
我们是七老八十吗 这么早吃饭
What are we, 80?

56
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,120
我们是二十几岁的小伙子吗 半夜才吃饭
What are we, 20?

57
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:11,073
接下来 第二个奇迹
Then...miracle number two.

58
00:02:11,073 --> 00:02:14,280
莉莉学前班里一个同学的妈妈
Turns out one of the mothers at Lily's pre-school

59
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,960
就是阿米莉亚本尊
is none other than Amelia herself.

60
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,420
所以我们约了她的儿子杰克逊一起玩
So we arranged a play date with her son, Jackson,

61
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:21,360
借机来取悦阿米莉亚
where we would, you know, charm Amelia.

62
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,140
好了
Okay.

63
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,120
史上最重要的游戏聚会
The most important play date ever,

64
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,960
所以你得表现出耀眼的一面哦 小甜心
so I'm really gonna need you to sparkle, sweetie.

65
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,620
我会像国庆日那天的烟火一样耀眼
Oh, I'm gonna sparkle like it's the 4th of July.

66
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:30,360
我是冲莉莉说的
I was talking to Lily.

67
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,740
今天是我们爸妈的结婚纪念日
It's our parents' anniversary,

68
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:34,500
我们准备把早餐给他们送到床头 给他们一个惊喜
so we're surprising them with breakfast in bed.

69
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,220
给他们买什么礼物 他们都不会喜欢的
They're impossible to buy for...

70
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:37,640
我们是这么想的
We think.

71
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,760
但我们也没买过
We've never really tried.

72
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,280
好了 准备好了吗
Okay. Ready?

73
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,360
一 二 三
One, two, three...

74
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,133
惊喜啊啊啊
Surpri-i-i--

75
00:02:48,133 --> 00:02:49,651
不 不
Oh. Oh! No! No!

76
00:02:49,651 --> 00:02:51,460
不 不 不
No! No! No!

77
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,420
-对不起 -什么都没发生
- I'm sorry! - Nothing's happening!

78
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,580
我的天啊
Oh, my god.

79
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,440
没错 孩子们撞见我们了
Yeah, our kids walked in on us.

80
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:59,640
-委婉地说 我们当时正在做爱 -天啊
- We were, as they say, "having sex." - Oh, god.

81
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,820
这一点也不委婉啊 菲尔
That's not a euphemism, Phil.

82
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:03,569
我们当时确实也就是在做爱
It's exactly what we were doing -- having sex.

83
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,780
还当着孩子们的面
In front of our children.

84
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,540
我们开始的时候他们又不在
Well, they weren't there when we started.

85
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:06,940
的确
No.

86
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:11,180
事实上 我们刚开始的时候 你也不在状态
In fact, you weren't even there when we sta...

87
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,580
天啊 天啊
Oh, my god. Oh, my god.

88
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,620
没什么大不了的 没准他们什么都没看见呢
It's okay. Maybe they didn't see anything.

89
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,620
亲爱的 他们尖叫 还把一托盘的早餐都扔了
Sweetie, t-they screamed, they dropped a tray of dishes,

90
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,400
然后就像屁股着火了一样地冲出去了
and then they ran out of here like they were on fire.

91
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,460
你才像着火一般火辣呢 女士
You were on fire, lady.

92
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,860
不是吧 你还有心情
Really? You're still going?

93
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,120
请原谅我认为
Well, forgive me for thinking

94
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,220
你如此激情的表现应该得到夸奖
your zesty performance deserves some praise.

95
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,720
菲尔 咱们的孩子现在正在楼下
Phil, our children are downstairs right now,

96
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,000
心灵上可能受到了巨大的创伤
and they are probably traumatized.

97
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,240
拜托 肯定没那么严重
Oh, come on. I'm sure it's not that bad.

98
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,380
我还是能看到
I can still see it!

99
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,800
我不敢相信刚刚发生的一切
I can't believe that just happened!

100
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,740
-他们刚才在干什么 -什么都没干
- What were they doing? - Nothing!

101
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:42,360
不管是什么都好 看上去老爸要赢了
Whatever it was, it looked like dad was winning.

102
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,720
是那个 他们在做那个
It! They were doing it!

103
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,000
他完全不明白你在说什么
He has no idea what you're taking about.

104
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
-性爱吗 -没错
- Sex? - Yes!

105
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:50,380
我知道性爱是什么 艾丽克斯
I know what sex is, Alex.

106
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,700
就是一男一女脱掉内衣
It's when a man and a woman take off their underpants

107
00:03:52,709 --> 00:03:53,860
然后上床
and then get into the bed.

108
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:54,680
别再说了
Stop talking!

109
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,560
再给克莱尔打一次
Try Claire again.

110
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:00,160
手机没信号
I'm not getting a signal.

111
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:01,780
放松 我们会联系上她的
Relax. We'll get her.

112
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:05,140
矮子跟我说拉斯维加斯有一家餐厅
Hey, shorty told me about this restaurant in Vegas

113
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,420
在餐厅的正中
that's got a three-story wine tower

114
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:08,740
有个三层的红酒塔
right in the middle of it.

115
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,160
给客人倒酒的服务生绑着钢索飞来飞去
The guy who gets your wine flies around on a wire.

116
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,200
就像小飞侠彼得潘一样
Like the "Peter Pan".

117
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,200
不 不是像彼得潘
No. Not like the "Peter Pan".

118
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,560
这个地方档次很高
This is a high-end place.

119
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,160
是吗 世界上所有高级的餐厅里
Oh, yeah, because all the finest restaurants in the world

120
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,420
都有人拉着钢索飞来飞去
have people flying around on wires.

121
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:22,840
以前有个日本人把虾扔到你盘子里
You know, you used to go bananas

122
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:25,140
你都会抓狂到上蹿下跳
when a Japanese guy flipped a shrimp onto your plate.

123
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,440
你再看看你现在这副刀枪不入的样子
Now look at you.

124
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,060
-再给她打一次 -好吧
- Try her again. - Fine.

125
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,120
再跟你说一次 那餐厅不是像彼得潘那样的
And just so you know, it's not like Peter Pan.

126
00:04:30,128 --> 00:04:31,607
那些服务生不会穿紧身裤什么的
I mean, nobody wears tights or anything.

127
00:04:31,607 --> 00:04:33,040
如果他们什么都不穿
Well, if they're not wearing anything,

128
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,860
我可不想让他们在我的食物上飞来飞去
I don't want them flying over my food.

129
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:35,880
喂
Hello.

130
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:38,100
菲尔 是我 能让克莱尔接电话吗
Phil, it's me. Can I talk to Claire?

131
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,880
好的 稍等 杰
Yeah. One second, Jay.

132
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,280
-是你爸 -不不不 不接
- It's your dad. - No. No, no. Can't. Unh-unh.

133
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:43,780
她现在不想说话
She doesn't want to talk right now.

134
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:45,460
-完蛋了 -为什么
- Ay, no. - Why not?

135
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,340
她有点伤心过度
Uh, she's a little too upset.

136
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,720
菲尔 让她接电话
Phil, put her on.

137
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,740
他说他想
He says he wants to --

138
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,460
把电话挂掉
Hang up the phone.

139
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,760
抱歉 杰
I'm sorry, Jay.

140
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,700
她让我挂电话
She says I have to go.

141
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:58,360
虽然她是我亲生闺女
You know, she's my daughter and everything,

142
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:01,040
但那小子真该有点骨气
but that guy seriously needs to grow a pair.

143
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:02,640
我们尽力了
Well, we tried.

144
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,340
拉斯维加斯 我们来啦
Vegas, here we come.

145
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,700
掉头
Turn around the car.

146
00:05:09,389 --> 00:05:13,392
我这是自愿掉头 可不是被你逼的
Only 'cause I want to.

147
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,749
你们家太漂亮了
This is a-a beautiful home.

148
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,520
我超六十年代复古风
I love the throwback to the '60s.

149
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,100
只不过如果现在真是六十年代的话
Although if this was the '60s,

150
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,920
我们就是一对"坚定的独身主义者"
we'd be a couple of "confirmed bachelors",

151
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,320
则莉莉会是一只约克夏
and Lily would be a Yorkie.

152
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,660
而我则会继续被困在无爱的婚姻中
And I'd still be trapped in a loveless marriage.

153
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,080
艾米莉亚
Oh, Amelia.

154
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,620
你真风趣
Oh, you are funny!

155
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,080
我真的很喜欢你们
I really like you guys.

156
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,920
我还没有时间
I mean, I haven't had a lot of time

157
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:36,820
去见其他的家长
to meet the other parents.

158
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:39,140
我是单身妈妈 工作又忙
You know, single mom, hectic work schedule...

159
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:40,640
艾米莉亚 你是做什么工作的
Now, what do you do, Amelia?

160
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,580
我有几家餐厅
I own a few restaurants.

161
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,480
我最近在附近又开了一家
I just opened one nearby.

162
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:47,220
天呐 就是那家艾米莉亚餐厅吗
Oh, my gosh. Are you that Amelia?

163
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,860
天呐
Oh, my gosh!

164
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:51,900
我们听说那家餐厅很棒
We've heard wonderful things about the restaurant.

165
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:53,040
那里生意一定很好
It must be doing well.

166
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,780
我们一直都订不到位子
We can never seem to get a r -- a reservation.

167
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:56,880
-都进不去 -进不去
- Can't get in. - Can't.

168
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,380
这事好办
Oh, well, that's no problem.

169
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,520
下次你打电话时 就告诉他们
The next time you call, just tell them --

170
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,120
等一下
Oh. One second.

171
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,200
不好意思 告诉他们什么
Oh, I'm sorry. Tell them what?

172
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:03,660
喂
Hello?

173
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,860
你给他看了吗 他说什么
Well, did you show it to him? And what did he say?

174
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,240
好的 等一下
Okay. Uh, hold on a second.

175
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,720
我换个电话
I'm gonna switch phones.

176
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,260
不好意思 是餐厅的事
I'm sorry. It's the restaurant.

177
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,820
我失陪一下
Excuse me just a minute.

178
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,020
你刚才叫我们在订位时跟他们说某句话的
You said to tell them something.

179
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:18,960
你听见了吗
Did you hear that?

180
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,140
等我们知道该说什么了 就有特权了
When we know what to say, we're in.

181
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,800
太让人激动了
Oh! This is very exciting.

182
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,829
我还从没在餐厅里享受过特权
I've never had an in at a restaurant before.

183
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,560
也许我们一到 他们就会在门口迎接我们 还叫得出我们的名字
They'll probably greet us at the door by our names,

184
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,000
然后把我们带到我们最爱的桌前
show us to our favorite table...

185
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,660
我们可以随意变换菜单
They'll let us play fast and loose with the menu,

186
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:31,410
晚餐时点午饭的食物 午餐时点晚餐的食物
order lunch things for dinner, dinner things for lunch!

187
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,220
-没事 没事 没事 -卡梅隆
- It's fine. It's fine. It's fine. - Cameron!

188
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:36,480
-没事 -别动了
- It's fine. - Stop moving.

189
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,120
你还在吗
You there?

190
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,840
让他接电话
Put him on the phone.

191
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:40,700
是婴儿监护器 要关掉吗
Oh, that's the baby monitor. Should we turn it off?

192
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,220
你是哪位
Who am I speaking to?

193
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:44,900
好吧 坎贝尔先生
Well...Mr. Campbell,

194
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,760
你要把厨房那个非常贵的工作台面换掉
you need to replace the extremely expensive countertop

195
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,960
上次叫你手下的笨蛋工人来修冰箱
that one of your incompetent workers clearly ruined

196
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,020
结果他却把工作台面弄坏了
when he was supposed to be fixing the refrigerator.

197
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,040
这就是她这么成功的原因
Okay, this is why she's so successful.

198
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,060
严厉但却镇定
She's tough but calm.

199
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:58,000
因为我不是白痴
Because I'm not an idiot!!

200
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,300
我可是法律学毕业的
As is evidenced by my law degree,

201
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:03,080
你要是不在接下来的七十二小时内
which I will happily dust off and use to crush you in court

202
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,120
把它给我修好 换掉
if you don't fix it, replace it,

203
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,440
或是开赔款支票给我的话 我就上法庭告死你
or send me a check in the next 72 hours.

204
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,900
这样吧 你呆在那
You know what? Stay right there.

205
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:10,960
不要走
Don't move.

206
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,400
装作你刚才什么都没听见一样
Act like you weren't listening.

207
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,440
怎么装
What does that look like?

208
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,080
很抱歉
I'm so sorry.

209
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,940
我得去一下餐厅
I have to run down to the restaurant for a minute.

210
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,660
我都不好意思说出口
I really feel terrible asking,

211
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:22,887
但是你们介不介意
but do -- would you guys mind --

212
00:07:22,895 --> 00:07:25,000
-没问题 我们会帮你照看孩子 -好的
- Oh, it's not a problem. We'll watch the kids. - Okay.

213
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,700
没错 你去照料
Oh, yes, you go take care

214
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,220
你那间我们迫不及待
of that fabulous restaurant of yours

215
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:29,360
想要挤进去的餐厅
that we cannot wait to try.

216
00:07:29,372 --> 00:07:31,660
艾米莉亚 我们预约时要说什么
And when we do call, Amelia, you said to --

217
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:34,400
杰克逊 妈妈一会就回来
Jackson, mommy will be right back.

218
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:35,900
真是太谢谢你们了
Okay. Thanks, you guys, so much.

219
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:36,700
我欠你们个大人情
I owe you big time.

220
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,660
听到了吗
Did you hear that?

221
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,200
她说欠了我们很大的人情
She owes us big time.

222
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,580
拉斯维加斯那间斟酒服务生挂着钢丝
You know, she also has that restaurant in Las Vegas

223
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,160
飞来飞去的餐厅也是她开的
where the sommeliers fly around on wires.

224
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:51,400
天呐 莉莉 谢谢你这么讨那边那位
Oh, my gosh. Lily, thank you for being such a trouper

225
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,620
不说话的小家伙的喜欢
with Mr. Personality over there.

226
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,840
我要好好地奖励你一下
I'm gonna get you a treat.

227
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:58,375
一盒果汁漏了 里面都湿了
Oh, a juice box broke in here. It's all wet inside.

228
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,240
你用得着那么大惊小怪吗 只是一片尿片
Will you stop gasping? It's just a diaper --

229
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,640
好吧 我们得想个计划
Okay. We need a game plan.

230
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,060
我们要排练一下到底要说什么
We need to rehearse exactly what we're gonna say

231
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,760
因为当我的宝贝孩子们用批判
because that is the only way I'm gonna hold it together

232
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,040
和厌恶的眼神望着我时
when my babies are looking at me

233
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,700
那是唯一能让我不会崩溃的办法了
with judgment and disgust.

234
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,540
首先 他们一直都是那样看我们的
First of all, that's how they always look at us.

235
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:23,500
菲尔
Oh, Phil.

236
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,660
其次 他们受的创伤没有你想象的那么大
Secondly, this isn't as traumatic as you think.

237
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:28,000
亲爱的 我有一次也曾撞见我爸妈做爱
Honey, I walked in on my parents having sex once.

238
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,710
那简直 太糟糕了
It was -- oh -- awful.

239
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,400
我甚至没法把那个画面从我的脑海里抹去
I can't even get the image out of my mind.

240
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,720
克莱尔 我们不像你的父母 咱俩状态好多了
Claire, we're not your parents. We're in much better shape.

241
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:35,920
好吧 你知道最糟糕的是什么吗
Okay. You want to know the worst thing?

242
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:37,920
他们连谈都不跟我谈
They didn't even talk about it.

243
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,260
他们就让那件事悬在那
They just let it hang there.

244
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,400
我不会那样对我们的孩子
I'm not gonna do that to our kids.

245
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:43,220
菲尔
Phil, this --

246
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:45,660
这是我们作为家长的关键性时刻
this is a defining moment for us as parents.

247
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:48,320
我们对这件事的处理方式
How we handle this could shape how they feel

248
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,100
会影响他们余生对性和亲密的看法
about sex and intimacy for the rest of their lives!

249
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:50,680
克莱尔 亲爱的
Claire. Honey.

250
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:52,940
亲爱的 只要咱俩不小题大做 这就不是什么大事
Honey, this is only a big deal if we make it a big deal.

251
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,780
这件事的基调是咱俩定的 冷静对待就是了
We set the tone here. So let's just play it cool.

252
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,260
就把这当成是一个有趣的大混战
Act like it was a big, funny mix-up.

253
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:58,840
说几个笑话 缓和一下气氛
Crack a few jokes. Lighten the mood.

254
00:08:59,360 --> 00:08:59,380
笑话
Jokes.

255
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:01,780
怎样的笑话
What kind of jokes?

256
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,740
这是
Well, this is...

257
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:04,694
我先随便举个例子
I'm just spitballin' here, but --

258
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:07,540
如果我说 敲门敲门
What if I was all, "Knock, knock"...

259
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,480
他们会说 是谁啊
and they were like, "Who's there"?

260
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,300
我就说 不想撞到
And I was all, "Someone who doesn't want to see

261
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,640
自己父母嘿咻的人
their parents doing it.

262
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,140
所以我们才敲门
That's why we knocked".

263
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:17,660
当然这还要修改一下
Again, this is -- this is very rough.

264
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,160
他们怎么还在楼上
Why are they still up there?

265
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,680
嘿咻一般要多久
How long does sex take?

266
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,440
天呐 不要说了
Oh, my god. Stop talking.

267
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,040
你们俩注意到了吗
Did you guys notice

268
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:26,760
老爸刚才的表情就像是
that dad had the same look on his face

269
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,220
看到了一款新车一样
as when he smells a new car?

270
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,240
我要离开
I need to leave.

271
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:32,540
我要去露营
I need to go to camp.

272
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,220
他们下来的时候肯定会很尴尬
This is gonna be so weird when they come down.

273
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:38,200
我们走吧 好吗 走吧
Let's just go. Okay? Come on.

274
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,520
等等 我饿了
Wait. But I'm hungry.

275
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,700
我们去买早餐 走吧 快走
We'll get breakfast. Let's just go. Come on!

276
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:45,360
走啊 快走
Let's go. Come on.

277
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:45,900
你们要去哪
Where are you going?

278
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:47,280
哪都行
Anywhere.

279
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:49,920
你妈妈在哪 我要跟她谈谈
Where is your mother? I need to talk to her.

280
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,520
我觉得这个时机不太合适
I don't think it's a good time right now.

281
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,460
她待在房间里不出来
She won't come out of her room.

282
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:54,980
她很郁闷 对吧
She's really upset, isn't she?

283
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,220
超郁闷
Big time.

284
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,040
你们怎么知道的
How'd you know?

285
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:57,720
我们打过电话来
We called.

286
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,180
告诉我她到底是怎么说的
Tell me exactly what she said.

287
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,500
我不知道 就听到她一直在叫
I don't know. There was just a lot of screaming.

288
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,760
发生这些事时 你爸爸在哪
Where was your father when all this was going on?

289
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:06,654
他就在她身后
Oh, he was right behind her.

290
00:10:10,027 --> 00:10:12,660
擦不掉 擦不掉
Oh! It's not coming out! It's not coming out!

291
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:14,080
要吸干那些果汁 不要擦 要吸
Blot! Don't rub! Blot!

292
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,520
我们已经过了吸污和抹擦的阶段了
We are beyond blotting and rubbing.

293
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,320
就等着一身大汗和痛哭流涕了
I think we've moved on to sweating and crying.

294
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,480
好了 好了 不要慌
Okay, okay. Let's not panic.

295
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,140
我们就对艾米莉亚实话实说
We'll just -- we'll tell Amelia what happened,

296
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,380
然后由我们负担清洗费
and then we'll pay to have it cleaned.

297
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,440
米奇尔 万一这个洗不掉怎么办
What if it can't be cleaned, Mitchell?!

298
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:25,660
好吧 那我们就赔她一块新的地毯
Okay, okay. Then we'll pay for a new rug.

299
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,060
你疯了吧
Are you insane?

300
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,560
我在《建筑学文摘》中看到过
I saw it in Architectural Digest.

301
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:35,620
一块卖5万美元 戴安·基顿家里也有一块
It cost $50,000. It was in Diane Keaton's house.

302
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,100
不是 是那个 那个叫什么名字
Oh, no, it was in, oh, what's-her-name's house.

303
00:10:38,118 --> 00:10:40,299
她演过《普里兹家族的荣誉》
Um, from "Prizzi's Honor".

304
00:10:40,299 --> 00:10:43,371
还有这个这个 《阿达一族》
From -- uh, oh, oh, she was in "Addams Family".

305
00:10:43,371 --> 00:10:44,026
你知道的 还有
You know, she --

306
00:10:44,026 --> 00:10:45,040
是安耶利卡·休斯顿
Anjelica Huston!

307
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:45,960
对对对
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

308
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:49,720
天哪 一块地毯卖五万美金
Oh! Oh, my god. $50,000 for a rug?!

309
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,040
小卡 我们哪有那么多钱
Cam, we don't have that kind of money.

310
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,400
也许她不会让我们赔
Maybe she won't make us pay.

311
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,240
想想看 假如有人弄脏了我们的地毯
I mean, we wouldn't make someone pay

312
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,160
我们也不会让人家赔的
if this happened to us.

313
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,760
你没听见她在电话里说的话吗
Did you not hear her on the phone?

314
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:59,480
给我修好它 换掉它 开赔款支票给我
"Fix it. Replace it. Write me a check".

315
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,280
她可能已经把这句话绣到枕头上了
She probably has that embroidered on a pillow.

316
00:11:01,299 --> 00:11:04,960
旁边就放了一罐人耳朵
Right next to a jar of human tears.

317
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,200
也许我们可以把它转一下[还有“逆转形势”的意思]
Maybe we can turn this around.

318
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,940
怎么弄 看上去就像有人在这流血了一样
How? It looks like someone bled out over here.

319
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:08,780
不 我说的是地毯
No. I mean the rug.

320
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:10,220
也许我们可以把整张地毯转一圈
Maybe we can turn the whole rug around,

321
00:11:10,220 --> 00:11:11,300
把这块污渍放到沙发底下
put it under the couch.

322
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,840
明白了吧 没人会发觉的
See? No one would ever know it's there.

323
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,800
天知 地知 你知 我知
Well, you know, we would know.

324
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:17,740
那么
Well...

325
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:19,800
你在想什么
What are you thinking?

326
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:21,320
你不会想知道的
You don't want to know.

327
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,392
不 说来听听吧 因为我
No, tell me, 'cause I'm --

328
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,100
我觉得我们想得一样
I think I'm thinking the same thing.

329
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,280
我深表怀疑
I seriously doubt that,

330
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,660
因为我在想刚才那个应该是琼·柯林斯[美国女演员]家
because now I'm thinking it was Joan Collins' house.

331
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:30,360
好吧
Okay.

332
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,256
很好
Great.

333
00:11:32,256 --> 00:11:35,313
歌洛莉亚 你 你来干吗
Gloria, what are you -- what are you doing here?

334
00:11:35,313 --> 00:11:37,080
慢着 孩子们呢
Wait, where are the kids?

335
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,040
他们刚刚出去了
They just left.

336
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,160
他们跟我说你很郁闷
They told me that you were very upset.

337
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,300
-天哪 -你完全有权郁闷
- Oh, god. -And you have every right to be.

338
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,480
这件事太可怕了
It was bad.

339
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:44,680
我知道
I know that.

340
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,980
克莱尔 这只是个意外
Claire, it was an accident.

341
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,440
那也无法改变它所造成的伤害
That doesn't make it any better.

342
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:51,000
好吧 你说的没错 我了解你的感受
Okay, you're right. I know how you feel.

343
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,360
-天哪 -我也曾遇到过这样的事
- Oh, god. - It happened to me before,

344
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,300
不过是和另外一个女人
with another woman.

345
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:56,060
而且那次我是受害者["被上的那个"]
And that time, I was the one getting it.

346
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:57,180
那感觉真的很难过[真的很疼]
And it hurt.

347
00:11:58,407 --> 00:12:00,420
很抱歉我如此直白
I'm sorry it had to come out like this,

348
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,960
但是你还是得承认
but you have to admit that you're only happy

349
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,580
只有当你是主导者的时候才会觉得开心
when you're the one cracking the whip.

350
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:05,180
你说啥
What?

351
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:06,560
别装了
